From 824b0386a5c5cda2206a76a1858b02b20a5846f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Farhan Riaz <its-forum@techlogix.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 03:05:07 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 03/11] core, desktop: Add opt-in memory reporting for loaded
 SWFs

Ruffle keeps one MovieLibrary per SwfMovie in a map that is weakly keyed
on the movie, so a movie's characters stay resident for exactly as long
as somebody holds a strong Arc<SwfMovie>. That makes "content was
unloaded but its memory was not returned" measurable, but only if the
state is actually walked, so add a reporter that does.

`--memory-report <FILE>` writes one CSV row per interval pairing the
process' resident set size with Ruffle's own accounting of every movie
still held: its characters, its bitmaps (both still-compressed and
decoded), its SWF data, and how many of its strong references come from
inside its own library rather than from anything that still needs it.

Off by default, and only walked when a report is being written.
